---
description: SAO Customer Challenge workshop. How to run the build and coach skills from Cursor.
alwaysApply: true
---

This repo is the SAO Customer Challenge. Participants read the README,
then their scenario, fill `worksheets/design-worksheet.md`, generate a starter agent,
and instrument it themselves.

In Claude Code the skills are slash commands. In Cursor they are these rules;
each rule includes the skill's own SKILL.md. Where a SKILL.md says `$ARGUMENTS`,
read the path or text the user gave in chat.

How to ask for things in this chat:
- "Build the agent for scenarios/<name>/brief.yaml on the langgraph path"
  → follow the build-agent-langgraph rule.
- "Build the agent ... on the python path" → build-agent-python rule.
- "Build the agent ... on the strands-mcp path" → build-agent-strands-mcp rule (advanced; not used in the challenge).
- "Coach agents/<folder>" → follow the coach rule. It reviews, it never fixes.

Hard rules that apply in every case:
- The generated agent's code must contain no observability code (no splunk_ao, galileo,
  opentelemetry, langsmith, langfuse imports; no code that reads SPLUNK_AO_, OTEL_ or
  GALILEO_ variables). The `.env` files may list the SPLUNK_AO_ placeholders.
  `python shared/check_skeleton.py <dir>` must print OK before you are done.
- While building the starter agent, never add evaluators, controls, alerts, or
  tracing to it. Point them at https://agent-observability-docs.splunk.com instead.
  Later, when the participant asks you to instrument their agent, follow
  `02-teach-mode.mdc`: coach, do not write the instrumentation.
- When anyone instruments an agent in this repo, the SDK is `splunk-ao`
  (`from splunk_ao import SplunkAOLogger`, `SPLUNK_AO_*` variables). Never the
  `galileo` package.
- Scaffold with `python shared/scaffold.py --skill <skill> --brief <brief.yaml> --out <dir>`,
  then edit only the blocks marked `# CUSTOMIZE:`.
